# MUTATION TESTING SCRATCH TREE.
#
# `mutmut run` COPIES the whole project to ./mutants and rewrites the package
# there into deliberately broken variants. It is build output, not source:
# regenerated every run, meaningless in a diff, and large.
#
# COMMITTING IT WOULD BE ACTIVELY HARMFUL rather than merely noisy -- a reviewer
# reading mutants/ sees code that is WRONG ON PURPOSE, and a grep across the
# repository would return the mutated variant beside the real one.
#
# mutmut-cicd-stats.json LIVES IN HERE TOO, and stays ignored for the same
# reason .artifacts/ is: it is the RESULT of one run on one machine, which is
# evidence-as-data, not source.
mutants/
.mutmut-cache

# Type checkers / linters
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pyre/
.pytype/
.ruff_cache/

# uv / poetry / pip
.uv-cache/
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# IDE / editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# Docker
.docker/

# EVIDENCE AS DATA, BUT NOT IN GIT.
#
# Gate runs emit structured evidence, verdicts and findings here. Those are
# FACTS ABOUT ONE EXECUTION on one machine at one moment -- the as-data half of
# the model -- and committing them would turn a record of what happened into a
# file that gets merged, conflicted, and eventually edited to say something
# convenient. CI publishes them as build artifacts instead.
.artifacts/

# Local artifacts
*.log
*.db
*.sqlite3
tmp/
.cache/

# Worktrees (created as siblings, but guard against in-repo placement)
worktrees/
